# C1-F2 (Doc 31 §1 W-C2): prettier is scoped to AUTHORED source under
# editors/vscode/** ONLY. Everything below is either a build artifact, a
# vendored dependency, an out-of-tree-but-locally-materialised test
# cache, or a spec-verbatim contributed artifact that MUST stay
# byte-identical to its normative source (Doc 21 grammar / Doc 22 §9
# snippets / the manifest) — none of it is hand-authored TS the
# formatting pass owns.

# Build output + the esbuild bundle (regenerated; never tracked).
out/
dist/

# Vendored deps + the @vscode/test-electron extension/user-data cache
# (the VS Code binary download is pinned out-of-tree to ~/.vscode-test
# by src/test/runTest.ts; this dir is the residual test profile — both
# are gitignored, neither is authored source).
node_modules/
.vscode-test/

# The packaged host-triple binaries (a build artifact; populate-bin.mjs).
bin/
*.vsix

# Spec-verbatim contributed artifacts — these mirror a normative spec
# byte-for-byte (Doc 21 TextMate grammar, Doc 22 §9 snippet bodies, the
# Marketplace manifest B1 owns); reformatting them would (a) churn a
# B1-owned file and (b) risk a spec-fidelity drift the V2 grammar /
# snippet Extension-Host tests assert verbatim. Out of C1-F2's scope.
syntaxes/
snippets/
assets/
package.json
package-lock.json
language-configuration.json
.eslintrc.json
.prettierrc.json
